hi this is pressure Locker in this video  we're going to end the debate on a  problem that commonly circulates around  the internet and usually generates a lot  of discussion  the problem is six minus one times zero  plus two divided by two some people say  the answer is seven and other people  strongly disagree and say the answer is  one so what's the answer this question  has some importance because in Canada  you actually have to solve this kind of  math problem to claim lottery or contest  prizes so let's try and figure it out  when we type the expression into Wolfram  Alpha we get the result of seven  similarly when we type it into Google it  also evaluates to the answer of seven  the disagreement comes because if you  type the same expression into an  old-school calculator it will evaluate  the result as being equal to one so  what's the correct answer well clearly  there's a potential for confusion and to  avoid that we need to come up with a  convention of how to evaluate these  expressions so there's only one answer  the acronym PEMDAS or bed moss is one  way to remember how we evaluate  expressions so we look at the things  that are in parentheses or brackets  first then exponents then we look at  multiplication and division and finally  addition and subtraction and otherwise  we go from left to right so for our  problem there is a multiplication one  times zero which needs to take  precedence that evaluates as 0 then  there's a division of 2 divided by 2  that needs to evaluate that evaluates  into 1 and finally we go left to right  so 6 minus 0 plus 1 is equal to 7 so the  correct answer to this expression is 7  and that's what we got in Wolfram Alpha  and Google and that's they got the  correct answer because they do  followed the order of operations on old  calculators it will just evaluate it  from left to right and that could end up  with the wrong answer so you always want  to be careful and followed the order of  operations I hope you like this video  please subscribe to my channel you can  support me on patreon catch me on my  blog mind your decisions on Twitter at  pressure Locker and you can get my books  listed on my website
 

